# Optional. Leave EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL out when the API runs on the same laptop as `npm run start`.
# While developing, the app then talks to the machine it was loaded from, on port 4000: the laptop's
# address on the Wi-Fi when Expo Go runs on a phone, `localhost` in a browser. It keeps working when the
# laptop moves to another network, which a fixed address in this file does not.
# Set it only when the API is somewhere else (a tunnel, another computer, a deployed server), then restart
# Metro with `npx expo start -c`, because the value is read when the app is bundled.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://<address-of-the-API>:4000
